t&quot; zones, subways, hospitals, colleges, zoos, and arcos which are actually cities in cities. You can now give names to places, and your city is surrounded by neighboring towns with which you can make trade. Finally, instead of the poll in the first game you now have the option of reading several newspapers to get an idea of your progress.","year":1989,"genre":["Simulation"],"cat":"MS-DOS","categoryType":"game","console":"msdos","origem":"MS-DOS","id":"DOS_8TVDC89YFP"}}